  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the given circuit, the equivalent resistance between the terminal A and B is ____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e22dc111-e69c-4bea-a268-14d7d5011a56-9894227.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 195px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "10",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e22dc111-e69c-4bea-a268-14d7d5011a56-9894227.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 195px;\" /></p><p>In the given circuit, both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> resistors&nbsp;get&nbsp;shorted out, thus no current will flow from them. Removing the resistors from which no current will flow.</p><p>Now, the circuit can be redrawn as shown below.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/7c2a49c7-822c-41f6-b1fd-e2dd0fd9a8f1-9894227_2.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 200px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>eq</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8214;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>eq</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>eq</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p>",
